Superstore Sales Performance Analysis (HNG Stage 0)

Project Overview
This project involves a comprehensive descriptive analysis of the "Superstore Sales" dataset. The primary goal was to explore retail data to identify key revenue drivers, customer behavior, and operational efficiency. By leveraging Microsoft Excel, I transformed raw transactional data into actionable business insights.

Key Business Questions Addressed:
Which product category and sub-category generate the most revenue?
Who are the top 10 highest-spending customers?
Which states are the most profitable for the business?
What is the most preferred shipping method among customers?
What is the total revenue generated across all global operations?

Technical Workflow
Data Cleaning:Handled missing values in sales and category entries.
              Removed duplicate records to ensure data integrity.
              Standardized numeric formats for financial calculation.

Data Analysis:Utilized Pivot Tables to aggregate sales by region, category, and time.
              Applied Excel formulas (SUMIFS, VLOOKUP, RANK) to identify top performers.

Data Visualization:Created dynamic Bar Charts and Pie Charts to visualize market share across Technology, Furniture, and Office Supplies.

Key Insights
Top Performer: The Technology category leads sales, contributing 36.5% of total revenue, driven largely by Phones.

Revenue Milestone: The business generated a total revenue of $2,265,425 USD.

Customer Loyalty: Identified the top 10 customers responsible for significant portions of the total spend, providing a basis for targeted loyalty programs.

Operational Trend: Identified the most frequently used shipping methods to help optimize logistics and supply chain costs.

Tools Used
Microsoft Excel: Data Cleaning, Pivot Tables, and Dashboarding.
